      "title": "The Measurement Enigma",
      "durationSeconds": 20,
      "startFrame": 1,
      "endFrame": 600,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "In classical physics, observing an object does not change its state. But in quantum mechanics, the very act of observation irreversibly changes what is being observed. This is the quantum measurement problem.",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "Classical observation is passive and non-invasive.",
          "startFrame": 1,
          "endFrame": 270
        },
        {
          "text": "In quantum mechanics, measurement irreversibly transforms the state.",
          "startFrame": 271,
          "endFrame": 600
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
